From 73c2fa69f2a9823cc6c3d72b8ec265f712102378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yohan <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backend: fix ML model path bug, make LLM provider
 Gemini-ready

ISSUE 1 - Local ML returning UNAVAILABLE (root cause found and fixed)

Traced getDefaultPredictor() -> loadSerializedModel() step by step per
the checklist:
  1. __dirname resolves correctly in both dev (tsx, src/analyzers) and
     prod (compiled dist/analyzers) - both are one level under the
     backend root, so `path.join(__dirname, "..", "..", "models", ...)`
     correctly reaches <backend>/models/tfidf-logistic-v1.json in both
     cases. Verified directly - not the bug.
  2/3/4/5. The bundled model file exists, reads, parses, and matches
     SerializedMlModel - verified by loading it directly. Not the bug.
  6/7/8. getDefaultPredictor()/predictPhishingProbability()/assessMl()
     are all correct and, once given a real model, produce a genuine
     finite 0-1 probability and AVAILABLE status. Verified directly.

Actual root cause: `modelPath ?? process.env.ML_MODEL_PATH ?? <default>`
only falls through on null/undefined. .env.example ships
`ML_MODEL_PATH=` (present, but blank) - dotenv sets
process.env.ML_MODEL_PATH to "" in that case, which is NOT
null/undefined, so the default bundled-model path was never reached.
fs.readFile("") then fails and is (correctly, by design) swallowed by
loadSerializedModel's catch block, producing a silent, misleading
UNAVAILABLE instead of a clear error.

Fix: src/analyzers/mlClassifier.ts now treats a blank/whitespace-only
value the same as unset for both the explicit modelPath argument and
process.env.ML_MODEL_PATH (a new firstNonBlank() helper), before
falling back to the bundled model path. No error-hiding introduced -
a genuinely missing/corrupt/malformed model file still correctly
returns null/UNAVAILABLE exactly as before; only the "present but
blank" case now behaves as "unset" instead of "empty path".

Reproduced the bug and verified the fix directly: with
ML_MODEL_PATH="", the previous code returned null; the fixed code
loads the real bundled tfidf-logistic-v1 model and produces a genuine
AVAILABLE result end-to-end through a live POST /scan + GET
/emails/:emailId (probability 0.83, classification "phishing").

ISSUE 2 - LLM / Gemini readiness

src/analyzers/aiAssessment.ts was already fully provider-agnostic (it
only calls provider.complete({system, user}) and parses the returned
text) - no changes needed there.

src/services/llmClient.ts was hardcoded to the Anthropic wire format
only, with no LLM_PROVIDER concept. Added:
  - createGeminiProvider(): builds a Gemini generateContent request
    (systemInstruction + contents parts) and parses
    candidates[0].content.parts[].text, mirroring the existing
    createAnthropicProvider() shape/options (including an injectable
    fetchImpl for testing).
  - llmProviderFromEnv() now branches on LLM_PROVIDER ("anthropic"
    default, "gemini" opt-in). LLM_PROVIDER unset behaves byte-for-byte
    identically to before (same Anthropic default URL/model) -
    Batch 4/5C/6 behavior is unchanged when no LLM_PROVIDER is set.
  - Gemini has NO hardcoded/default model name on purpose - LLM_MODEL
    must be set explicitly when LLM_PROVIDER=gemini, so this can never
    ship a Gemini model name that's already outdated.
  - No secrets hardcoded anywhere; .env.example documents LLM_PROVIDER
    and the Gemini setup shape (still with a blank LLM_API_KEY).

ISSUE 3 - Recommended Actions (Batch 5C) - investigated, NOT a bug

Traced the full pipeline live end-to-end (POST /scan -> GET
/emails/:emailId), including with the ML_MODEL_PATH="" bug
deliberately reproduced to check for a cascading failure:
  - Batch 5C's generateRecommendations() IS called and DOES generate
    actions (confirmed: WARN_RECIPIENT, REVIEW_BLOCK_DOMAIN for a
    phishing-style test email).
  - They ARE attached to the stored-record response as top-level
    `recommendations` on GET /api/v1/emails/:emailId (routes/emails.ts,
    unchanged from Batch 5C).
  - The field name is `recommendations`, and the frontend's
    emailMapper.ts (fixed in the previous frontend patch) already reads
    exactly that field into ScannedEmail.recommendedActions.
  - Recommendations do NOT depend on ML being AVAILABLE - deterministic
    risk/domain evidence alone is enough to trigger them, confirmed by
    reproducing with ML_MODEL_PATH="" and still getting both actions
    back correctly.
  - Empty recommendedActions is correct, by design, for a genuinely
    low-risk/fully-covered email (Batch 5C: "no forced recommendation")
    - this is not a bug even though it looks identical to "missing" in
      the UI.

No backend change was needed or made for this issue. One caveat found
during tracing, reported for awareness only (not fixed here, since it's
a pre-existing frontend-only gap outside a "backend problem" ticket):
Investigation-style pages (e.g. ForensicsPage.tsx) don't render
recommendedActions at all today - only the Scanner result view does
(from the prior frontend fix). If recommendations should also appear
there, that's a small, separate frontend addition.

Files changed:
  - src/analyzers/mlClassifier.ts (the actual fix)
  - src/services/llmClient.ts (Gemini provider + branch)
  - .env.example (documents LLM_PROVIDER and the blank-is-safe
    ML_MODEL_PATH default; no secrets)
  - tests/mlClassifier.test.ts (6 new regression tests for the blank
    modelPath/env-var bug, plus an end-to-end AVAILABLE-result test)
  - tests/llmClient.test.ts (new - 9 tests covering the Anthropic
    default, Gemini opt-in, missing-model-name rejection, and the
    Gemini request/response wire format)

Verification performed exactly as requested:
  1. .eml scan succeeds - yes (201).
  2. Local ML returns AVAILABLE - yes, even with ML_MODEL_PATH="".
  3. ML probability is genuine 0-1 - yes (0.8316753184615787 on the
     bundled model, not hardcoded).
  4. ML classification returned - yes ("phishing").
  5. Recommended Actions survive the pipeline - yes (2 actions,
     confirmed via the same live request).
  6. AI remains UNAVAILABLE only for lack of a configured API key -
     yes, confirmed; Gemini is now selectable via LLM_PROVIDER once a
     real key + model are set, nothing fabricated.
  7. npm run build - clean.
  8. npm test - 244/244 passing, no Batch 5C/6 functionality broken.

No secrets or API keys were created or committed.
